Tsingi wrote:
> Would a demon slaying Archon be any help against Rodney?

An Archon soon goes up to level 28, 228 hit points, and with any
reasonable equipment can kill the Wizard a few times; but Rodney gets
stronger each time he comes back, and therefore can become stronger
than an Archon.

Archons are stronger than almost any normal monster, but a purple worm
or a trapper can kill an Archon in one shot. Genocide is a good idea if
you plan to have a pet Archon. Fighting against unfriendly Archons, or
lots of strong monsters with no time to reast in between, can also kill
an Archon.

Archons can be tamed by a blindfolded (to avoid being confused) level
30 Wizard, but it may take quite a few tries. They can also summon
nasties, and the nasties can include more Archons! Due to this, I once
had more pet Archons than I could count, and ascended with 8 after
having lost a few of them.

Keep your Archons leashed if you have enough leashes. Keep a magic
whistle in main inventory. If you use a bullwhip to disarm a pet
Archon, do not drop the bullwhip on the floor! Archons are smart, and
may pick it up and disarm you!

Don't use Conflict.

You can probably tell that the pet Archon is one of my favorite things.
